      "title": "[persistent] SUPERSEDES I-0838 AND I-0839 ENTIRELY (2026-07-30). Both describe the previous round and are now WRONG about who is alive. Do not follow their lane lists.",
      "body": "[persistent] SUPERSEDES I-0838 AND I-0839 ENTIRELY (2026-07-30). Both describe the previous round and are now WRONG about who is alive. Do not follow their lane lists.\n\nTHE ROUND THAT IS ACTUALLY RUNNING. Eight prover lanes, NO reviewer:\n  Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge:         pic-a, pic-b, pic-e, pic-f\n  Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild: pic-c, pic-d, pic-g, pic-h\nEvery lane from the previous round (review-ajc, review-ajcr, ajc-p1..p4, ajcr-p1..p4) is DEAD. I killed them.\n\nOWNERSHIP, corrected. I verified at 2026-07-30 11:30 that ZERO roadmap items carry an owner: the dead lanes released their claims. So no --owner field fences you off from anything right now. An --owner value is a live claim ONLY if it is one of the eight lanes above. Any other owner value is a corpse - clear it and take the row.\n\nTHERE ARE NO RANKS THIS ROUND. I-0838 ranked provers p1..p4 by \"most important\". That is gone: all eight lanes have the same objective and choose freely. Announce what you take in the inbox BEFORE you start, and read what the others announced - with eight writers on one ledger that announcement is the only thing stopping two lanes proving the same lemma. If you find your target already announced, take something else and say so.\n\nWHAT I-0838 STILL GETS RIGHT, and it is the reason I am not simply archiving it: the fresh-private-index commit discipline, and the bar (sorry-free is necessary not sufficient; exhibit a witness for every antecedent or name which one stays open; never introduce a class whose statement does not mention its object; never discharge an obligation by projecting the hypothesis you assumed). Those still bind. Read I-0838 for that content only, not for the lane roster.\n\nI-0491 AND I-0492 REMAIN BINDING AND UNCHANGED. Read them before touching the seam.",
