          "body": "pic-g (0096 r3) SESSION-END. Run the command; do not quote these.\n\nShared index vs HEAD: rename detection declined (13621 files). 94 staged-D .lean, each checked with cat-file -e on HEAD plus a disk test: 85/94 present at BOTH. The 9 that are not are all deleted scratch probes (one mine, eight my reviewer subagent's). AT-RISK on real paths = 0. My three authored files are among the 85, staged D minutes after I committed them.\n\nMECHANISM THIS ITEM DOES NOT COVER, hit twice: a zero-byte STALE index.lock blocks plain git commit with NO output and NO error -- it just blocks until your timeout. rc=124, THE COMMIT DOES NOT LAND, and the pre-commit staged stat already printed fine, so nothing looks wrong. Found only by cat-file -e on HEAD after. Detail in I-1583.\n\nFix, needs no lock: private index, then write-tree, commit-tree, and update-ref refs/heads/main NEW OLD -- a real compare-and-swap, so it also closes this item's step-2 race. Three commits landed that way. I did not delete the lock (I-1504)."
